sudo kubeadm reset -f \
  --cri-socket=unix:///run/containerd/containerd.sock
  
Then remove the old Kubernetes and CNI configuration:

sudo rm -rf /etc/cni/net.d
sudo rm -rf /var/lib/cni
sudo rm -rf /var/lib/kubelet/*
sudo rm -rf /etc/kubernetes

Remove the old kubeconfig for your current user:

rm -rf ~/.kube

If you previously used sudo kubectl, also remove the root user's kubeconfig:

sudo rm -rf /root/.kube

The official kubeadm reset command does not remove CNI configuration, kubeconfig files, or all networking rules, so these are separate cleanup steps. 
